[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Shared fields inherited across every grammar file

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[WORK]
UID: WORK-GRAMMAR-FIELD-INHERITANCE
TITLE: Shared fields inherited across every grammar file
DEPTH: sketch
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
A set of shared fields present on every node in every grammar file;
authorship (AUTHORED_BY) is the operator's example. The Nix grammar layer
(values.nix / packages/strictdoc-grammar, where the .sgra files are rendered
from) fans them out: a helper that adds the subset to every grammar, or,
as the MVP, the consumer adds them by hand. First-party strictdoc support
would be nicer. This is about reused fields only. It is NOT the delivery
mechanism for annotations (WORK-ANNOTATION-NODES) and has nothing to do
with them.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
Verbatim: "inheritance - nix special tooling. like authorship across all
nodes all grammars." Read as: shared field/semantic definitions composed
into each rendered grammar, not strictdoc-level inheritance. Flag if wrong.

Operator, 2026-09-01, verbatim: "field inheritance was meant like all
nodes, in any grammar. nix fans out (like a subset of fields added to
every grammar with a helper or even the consumer could just do it mvp)
but first-party support would be nice. this is for reused fields like
authorship, nothing to do with annotations itself."

Changed 2026-09-01: the earlier reading "not strictdoc-level inheritance"
is amended -- Nix fan-out is the route (helper, or by hand as MVP), and
first-party strictdoc support is the nicer end state, not excluded. Neither
the STATEMENT nor these NOTES tied this item to annotations; the
clarification confirms there is no such tie, and the STATEMENT now says so.
<<<
